> For an spde problem, I am trying to increase the number of cores used in a multicore system with the inla( ..., num.threads=XX ) option. It seems to permit the number of cores to be altered from 1 to 4, but no higher. Using the inla.setOption(num.threads=XX) approach provides the same behaviour. I am wondering if this is normal behaviour and if so, would there be a work-around? I have plenty of RAM.

What is the symptom you experience?  Does it simply not "go faster" or do you get an error?
"Plenty of RAM" is also relative to the actual model; space-time models for example can easily use tens of GB ram if you're not careful.  The part mostly affected by multiple threads is the integration stage. The optimization stage is more serial in nature, so if your problem is dominated by that stage there's a practical limit to how much benefit you can get from multiple threads.

Finn L

