As far as I know, the default build should allow more than 4 threads.  But it's possible that the optimization stage doesn't have a practical use for more than 4 cores; you can test this by running a smaller problem, and make sure to use verbose=TRUE.  The integration stage should use all the threads, so that will tell you how many threads it is using, even if the optimization cannot take full advantage of them.

Finn

